{"name":"Light Youth","hex":"#ead7d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"youth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The quality or state of being young.","The part of life following childhood; the period of existence preceding maturity or age; the whole early part of life, from childhood, or, sometimes, from infancy, to adulthood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/youth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Youth","blocks":[{"text":"Youth is the time of life when one is young. The word, youth, can also mean the time between childhood and adulthood (maturity), but it can also refer to one's peak, in terms of health or the period of life known as being a young adult. Youth is also defined as \"the appearance, freshness, vigor, spirit, etc., characteristic of one, who is young\". Its definitions of a specific age range varies, as youth is not defined chronologically as a stage that can be tied to specific age ranges; nor can its end point be linked to specific activities, such as taking unpaid work, or having sexual relations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/1970sgirls.jpg/330px-1970sgirls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Youth","wikidata":"Q190007"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Two_Irish_High_School_Girls.jpg/500px-Two_Irish_High_School_Girls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Two_Irish_High_School_Girls.jpg/500px-Two_Irish_High_School_Girls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two Irish secondary school-aged girls at a picnic table","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwo_Irish_High_School_Girls.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Tides_Class_Stallings-1_%289719204532%29.jpg/500px-Tides_Class_Stallings-1_%289719204532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Tides_Class_Stallings-1_%289719204532%29.jpg/1280px-Tides_Class_Stallings-1_%289719204532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Tides_Class_Stallings-1_%289719204532%29.jpg/500px-Tides_Class_Stallings-1_%289719204532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Students of a U.S. university do an outdoor class, where they discuss topics while walking.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATides_Class_Stallings-1_(9719204532).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo